can use this fact to compute ${B}^{5}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{5} & ={B}^{2}\\cdot {B}^{2}\\cdot B \\\\  & =B\\cdot B\\cdot B \\\\  & ={B}^{2}\\cdot B \\\\  & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & ={B}^{2} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{B}^{5}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440932 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02156f42-01b9-5208-be76-46dd56d1f051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440906} {:answer/id #uuid "6988567e-c6b3-5730-a2d4-b0c476a8c21a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440912} {:answer/id #uuid "79b811ba-d237-5358-9a7b-e5099ee68347" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440913} {:answer/id #uuid "c40a1344-3c43-5a5d-97e2-770817ab45f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440921} {:answer/id #uuid "fb87aec8-67bb-5868-9fd5-615026521a6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440925}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440913} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2b3e7c5-52c2-5e4b-bcbf-08cf2d113f06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "de50db69-1f49-5b62-bb8f-7cba652094a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-130663" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${A}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${A}^{2}=A,$ so $A$ is an idempotent matrix. \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${A}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & ={A}^{2} \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{A}^{4}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of an Idempotent Matrix"}] :topic/math-academy-id 3776 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049408} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049489}] :topic/title "Nilpotent and Idempotent Matrices"}
